Cell["6. Cancellation-factor families and boundary closures", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2f78ab6c-e88b-4da9-a78e-bdacc0312329"],

Cell["\<\
Across the 0 staged candidates, the number of cancellation factors per \
candidate has profile <||>. Part I returns one generator per candidate; in \
these samples each generator factors into two of the reported cancellation \
factors. After canonicalising overall signs and normalisations, there are 0 \
distinct cancellation-factor polynomials and 0 distinct product generators. \
The identity of the factor set or generator is therefore a useful family \
label; the factor count alone need not be.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"70fbd91b-ad79-4606-8651-b1a40a4459c3"],

